I found no rendering or timing defect and made no source edits. The report starts with FINDINGS rather than PASS because I didn't run the full `tests/verify.sh`, and some checks can't be done headless.

- **Cold starts:** I ran 8 fresh headless Chromium sessions with an empty cache, 4 at normal speed and 4 with 4x CPU throttling. The first frame and first tic arrive at about 156–161 ms normally and 215–220 ms throttled.
- **Tic rate:** measured from the first tic, it was 35.0/s in 7 of the 8 runs and 34.7/s in the other.
- **Frames:** every canvas pixel was opaque in all runs, and there were no page errors.
- **Reviewer's low first reading:** the engine holds 35 tics/s from its first tic, so there's no ramp-up in my code. The 17–23/s readings probably came from load latency in the reviewer's session. I couldn't reproduce that, so the cause is not proven.
- **Source identity:** same revision as the previous reports. The `git diff HEAD` hash starts c9b3c829ca2c5a67 and `dist/doom.wasm` starts 7afb94fa1ec64b5c. My three files are unchanged, and I didn't rebuild.
- **Still open:**
  - Real hidden-tab timing, which a human needs to check (H1 in `tests/README.md`).
  - Firefox, Safari and a physical HiDPI display.
  - A full `tests/verify.sh` run on this revision.

